                      (        forth.asm):01164         
                      (        forth.asm):01165         * FDCTSYM enveadours to match the address stored in Y to a dictionary entry.
                      (        forth.asm):01166         * Upon a successful flexible match, it will output a string in the form of
                      (        forth.asm):01167         * <wordname>+<offset> to the string pointed to by X. <wordname> refers to the
                      (        forth.asm):01168         * code entry point of the matched word. <offset> will be expressed in hex.
                      (        forth.asm):01169         * If a match is found, Z will be clear, otherwise it will be set.
                      (        forth.asm):01170         * A candidate for a word code address must meet the following criteria:
                      (        forth.asm):01171         * ((Y U>= #EBUFS) AND (Y U< #THEEND)) OR ((Y U>= #WDICSPC) AND (Y U< DICEND)).
                      (        forth.asm):01172         * Upon return:
                      (        forth.asm):01173         * - the string pointed to by X will updated with its symbolic match
