                      (        forth.asm):04089         * The algorithm implemented here is similar to Donald's Knuth algorithm M,
                      (        forth.asm):04090         * as described in "The Art of Computer Programming", Volume II, 3rd edition,
                      (        forth.asm):04091         * section 4.3.1, pp 268. It is not as generic as algorithm M but fits our
                      (        forth.asm):04092         * particular purpose here: a 16x16 bit unsigned multiplication that yields
                      (        forth.asm):04093         * a 32 bit result. A simpler description of algorithm M can be found in
                      (        forth.asm):04094         * Henry S. Warren Junior's "Hacker's Delight", second edition, section 8-1,
                      (        forth.asm):04095         * pp 171. A C prototype implementation for a little endian host is provided
                      (        forth.asm):04096         * in SW/util/umstar.c.
                      (        forth.asm):04097         * In essence we reduce the problem to a 2 digit by 2 digit (expressed in
                      (        forth.asm):04098         * base 256) multiplication and use the 6809 MUL (A * B -> D) instruction.
DCE6 03               (        forth.asm):04099         UMSTAR  fcb     3               ANSI (Core)
