DCEA DCDB             (        forth.asm):04101                 fdb     MSTAR
DCEC C7               (        forth.asm):04102                 RFCS
DCED BDCC34           (        forth.asm):04103 (7)             jsr     MIN2PST         2 parameters need to be stacked up
                      (        forth.asm):04104         * Register allocation notes:
                      (        forth.asm):04105         * X: pointer to ud1 (ARG_U/p in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04106         * Y: pointer to ud2 (ARG_V/q in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04107         * E: Inner loop index (i in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04108         * F: Outer loop index (j in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04109         *
                      (        forth.asm):04110         * We save U to the system stack and use it to point to a scratch area allocated
                      (        forth.asm):04111         * from the system stack that will contain the 4 bytes (double cell) ultimately
                      (        forth.asm):04112         * holding the result (MSB first, what else?).
                      (        forth.asm):04113         *
                      (        forth.asm):04114         * System stack structure:
                      (        forth.asm):04115         * ,S    Result scratch area (Result MSB)
                      (        forth.asm):04116         * 2,S   Result scratch area (Result LSB)
                      (        forth.asm):04117         * 4,S   Saved U register
